360 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E(On the 8th of April 1975 the club would receive a visit from FC Barcelona, who had originally been intended to train at Bradford City\220s Valley Parade stadium before their semi-final match of the European Cup against Leeds United, but due to a mix-up, there was a game being played there causing Barcelona to be turned away. A Bradford City representative gave them the number of Stewart Willingham, Thackley's secretary at the time, after a conversation between Stewart and a UK Barcelona representative. Both parties made their way to Dennyfield, where the pitch would open for Barcelona to train. The training session did not serve them well as Leeds United beat them 2-1.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[13 484 0 R 15 485 0 R 17 486 0 R 19 487 0 R 21 488 0 R 23 489 0 R 25]>>
endobj

